WASHINGTON, D.C. - Today, Congressman Marc Veasey (TX-33) announced the launch of his newly revamped website designed to better serve his constituents in the 33rd Congressional District of Texas.
“Constituent services are a hallmark priority of my office,” said Congressman Veasey. “My goal is to remove every barrier that stands in the way of my constituents’ access to services provided by my office and information about what I’m doing on their behalf.”  
The new website includes:
 A prominently displayed “How Can I Help You?” section on the homepage with links to the most frequently-asked constituent services;
	An emphasis on digital media such as Facebook and Twitter, with easy-access to all of the Congressman's digital media platforms;
	A new “Newsroom” which includes links to the latest news stories, announcements and video messages relevant to the district.
	An updated issue section directing constituents to information most relevant to the district;
	And a robust interactive advanced search tool.
 To check out the new website visit,  https://veasey.house.gov/
